This repository contains original scripts, measurements and documentation.

It does NOT redistribute any upstream source and does NOT redistribute model weights.
`patches/gbnf_pattern_fix.py` is an original litellm callback module written for this rig;
it is included so the ordered-ceiling and output-clamp behaviour described in README.md is
reproducible, not as a redistribution of litellm.

Upstream projects referenced:
  vLLM                              Apache-2.0   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
  litellm                           MIT          https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm
  Qwen3.8-27B                       see model card on HuggingFace (Qwen)
  Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-NVFP4      see model card on HuggingFace (orcarouter); abliterated
                                    per Arditi et al. (2024), "Refusal in Language Models Is
                                    Mediated by a Single Direction", then quantized to mixed
                                    NVFP4 + FP8 with llmcompressor
  mini-swe-agent / SWE-bench Pro    see their respective repositories

The referenced checkpoint is an abliterated (refusal-removed) model. This repository
documents serving configuration and performance measurement only. It is published to
support authorized security testing, red-team evaluation and refusal-mechanism research in
isolated environments, and contains no harmful content, jailbreak material, or capability
demonstrations. Anyone deploying such a checkpoint is responsible for providing independent
safety and moderation layers; the publisher's own card states it has no meaningful built-in
guardrails.

Third-party benchmark figures attributed to Nathan Sapwell (nathan.sapwell.net) are cited,
not reproduced, and are that author's measurements rather than ours. Where cited they refer
to the FP8 build of this abliteration, not the NVFP4 checkpoint served here.

Benchmark numbers in this repository were measured on the author's own hardware and are
reported as measured, including the runs that failed and the measurements that turned out
to be wrong.
